    <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Does GPSR actually apply to clothing, or just electronics and toys?</h3>
      <p>Yes, it applies to clothing. GPSR covers any consumer product sold in the EU that doesn't have its own dedicated safety law — toys and electronics have separate directives, but clothing and footwear fall under GPSR by default. Since 13 December 2024, that means a risk assessment, traceability information, and an EU Responsible Person are required for garments sold to EU consumers, whether through your own store or a marketplace such as Amazon.de or Zalando.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3 style="margin-top:0;">What exactly needs to be in a GPSR risk assessment for a t-shirt or hoodie?</h3>
      <p>It needs to cover physical risks (drawstrings, small attached parts, sharp trims), chemical risks (dyes, prints, finishes), and foreseeable misuse — for example, a child's hoodie with a long drawstring. The assessment should record what was checked, what guidance was used, and what action was taken. A one or two page record per style, kept on file for ten years, is the practical minimum most brands use.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Can a factory in Bangladesh act as my EU Responsible Person?</h3>
      <p>No. The role must be filled by a company or individual physically established within the EU or Northern Ireland — a factory in Bangladesh cannot take this on, regardless of certifications held. Most non-EU brands use a paid Responsible Person service, an EU fulfilment partner, or an existing EU subsidiary or distributor.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3 style="margin-top:0;">What is the actual penalty if my clothing brand isn't GPSR compliant?</h3>
      <p>Enforcement varies by member state, but the most common real-world consequence for smaller brands is listing removal from marketplaces like Amazon or Zalando, since these platforms now request GPSR documentation during seller onboarding and periodic reviews. Customs holds at EU ports and fines from national market surveillance authorities are also possible, depending on the country.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3 style="margin-top:0;">What is the EU Digital Product Passport and when do clothing brands need one?</h3>
      <p>It's a digital record, accessed via a QR code or similar, that will show a garment's material composition, origin, and recyclability data — part of the ESPR framework. For textiles, the detailed rules are still being finalised, with finalisation expected around 2026–2027 and enforcement anticipated from roughly 2027–2028. Brands don't need one today, but recording fabric origin and fibre composition now makes the eventual transition much easier.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3 style="margin-top:0;">Does Bangladesh sourcing still make sense given all these new EU rules?</h3>
      <p>Yes — these rules apply regardless of sourcing country, so they aren't a Bangladesh-specific hurdle. Bangladesh retains 0% EU import duty under EBA, versus roughly 12% for China. A factory already holding GOTS, OEKO-TEX, and BSCI certifications generally has most of the documentation a GPSR technical file needs already in place.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="disclaimer-box">
      This tool provides a general readiness indicator based on publicly available EU regulatory information as of June 2026 and is not legal advice. Regulations, delegated acts, and enforcement practices change — confirm current requirements with a qualified compliance advisor or your EU Responsible Person before making commercial decisions. SDF Clothing is a garment manufacturer, not a legal or compliance consultancy.
    </div>

  </div>

</div>

<script>
  const TOTAL_QUESTIONS = 18;
  const answers = {};

  const checkBtn = document.getElementById('check-btn');
  const validationMsg = document.getElementById('validation-msg');
  const remainingCount = document.getElementById('remaining-count');
  const progressFill = document.getElementById('progress-fill');
  const progressCount = document.getElementById('progress-count');

  function updateProgress() {
    const answeredCount = Object.keys(answers).length;
    progressCount.textContent = String(answeredCount);
    progressFill.style.width = ((answeredCount / TOTAL_QUESTIONS) * 100) + '%';

    if (answeredCount >= 12) {
      checkBtn.disabled = false;
      validationMsg.classList.remove('visible');
    } else {
      checkBtn.disabled = true;
      const remaining = 12 - answeredCount;
      remainingCount.textContent = String(remaining) + (remaining === 1 ? ' question' : ' questions');
      if (answeredCount > 0) {
        validationMsg.classList.add('visible');
      }
    }
  }

  document.querySelectorAll('.q-block').forEach((block) => {
    const qId = block.getAttribute('data-qid');
    block.querySelectorAll('.q-btn').forEach((btn) => {
      btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const val = btn.getAttribute('data-val');
        answers[qId] = val;

        block.querySelectorAll('.q-btn').forEach((b) => {
          b.classList.remove('sel-yes', 'sel-no', 'sel-partial');
        });

        const selClass = val === 'yes' ? 'sel-yes' : val === 'no' ? 'sel-no' : 'sel-partial';
        btn.classList.add(selClass);

        block.classList.remove('answered-yes', 'answered-no', 'answered-partial');
        const stateClass = val === 'yes' ? 'answered-yes' : val === 'no' ? 'answered-no' : 'answered-partial';
        block.classList.add(stateClass);

        updateProgress();
      });
    });
  });

  function scoreGroup(ids) {
    let total = 0;
    ids.forEach((id) => {
      if (answers[id] === 'yes') total += 1;
      else if (answers[id] === 'partial') total += 0.5;
    });
    return Math.round((total / ids.length) * 100);
  }

  function barColor(pct) {
    if (pct >= 75) return '#4ade80';
    if (pct >= 50) return '#facc15';
    return '#e00';
  }

  function buildAction(priority, title, description, link) {
    return { priority, title, description, link };
  }

  checkBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
    if (Object.keys(answers).length < 12) return;

    const gpsr = scoreGroup(['q1', 'q2', 'q3', 'q4']);
    const reach = scoreGroup(['q5', 'q6']);
    const labelling = scoreGroup(['q7', 'q8', 'q9']);
    const espr = scoreGroup(['q10', 'q11', 'q12']);
    const factory = scoreGroup(['q13', 'q14', 'q15', 'q16', 'q17', 'q18']);

    const answeredIds = Object.keys(answers);
    let totalScore = 0;
    answeredIds.forEach((id) => {
      if (answers[id] === 'yes') totalScore += 1;
      else if (answers[id] === 'partial') totalScore += 0.5;
    });
    const overall = Math.round((totalScore / answeredIds.length) * 100);

    const scoreNum = document.getElementById('score-num');
    const scoreCircle = document.getElementById('score-circle');
    scoreNum.textContent = overall + '%';
    scoreCircle.style.borderColor = barColor(overall);

    const verdicts = [
      [80, 'Strong GPSR Readiness', 'Most core requirements are in place. Close the remaining gaps below before your next EU shipment or marketplace review.'],
      [55, 'Partial Readiness', 'A foundation exists, but the gaps below include items that can block EU retail or marketplace onboarding on their own.'],
      [30, 'Significant Gaps', 'Multiple core GPSR requirements are not yet met. Address the EU Responsible Person, risk assessment, and labelling items before continuing EU sales.'],
      [0, 'Not Yet GPSR Ready', 'Core GPSR requirements are missing. Work through the action plan below before listing products for sale in the EU.']
    ];
    const verdictMatch = verdicts.find(([min]) => overall >= min);
    document.getElementById('score-verdict').textContent = verdictMatch[1];
    document.getElementById('score-sub').textContent = verdictMatch[2];

    const categoryBars = [
      ['gpsr', gpsr], ['reach', reach], ['label', labelling], ['espr', espr], ['factory', factory]
    ];
    categoryBars.forEach(([key, pct]) => {
      const fillEl = document.getElementById('bar-' + key);
      const pctEl = document.getElementById('pct-' + key);
      fillEl.style.width = pct + '%';
      fillEl.style.background = barColor(pct);
      pctEl.textContent = pct + '%';
    });

    const actions = [];
    if (answers['q3'] === 'no') actions.push(buildAction('critical', 'Appoint an EU Responsible Person', 'Brands based outside the EU cannot legally sell into the EU without an appointed EU Responsible Person under GPSR. Their contact details must appear on your product or packaging.', null));
    if (answers['q1'] === 'no') actions.push(buildAction('critical', 'Write a risk assessment for each EU-bound style', 'GPSR requires a documented risk assessment covering physical, chemical, and misuse risks per style. Without this, EU market surveillance authorities can block or recall affected products.', null));
    if (answers['q5'] === 'no') actions.push(buildAction('critical', 'Get fabrics tested or switch to OEKO-TEX certified fabric', 'Selling garments containing restricted substances is a serious compliance breach. Commission accredited lab testing, or move to OEKO-TEX certified fabric as a faster route.', '/contact'));
    if (answers['q17'] === 'no') actions.push(buildAction('critical', 'Review and remove unsupported sustainability claims', 'Terms like "eco-friendly" or "sustainable collection" without certified evidence are restricted under EU rules on environmental claims. Remove the wording or obtain GOTS/GRS certification before your next shipment.', null));
    if (answers['q7'] === 'no' || answers['q7'] === 'partial') actions.push(buildAction('warning', 'Update fibre content labels to official EU fibre names', 'Regulation 1007/2011 requires the legal fibre name, not a marketing name. Review label templates before your next production run.', '/contact'));
    if (answers['q2'] === 'no') actions.push(buildAction('warning', 'Add responsible-business contact details to labels or packaging', 'GPSR requires a name and contact address for the manufacturer or importer to be shown on or with every product.', null));
    if (answers['q8'] === 'partial' || answers['q8'] === 'no') actions.push(buildAction('warning', 'Add labels in the language of each EU market you sell in', 'Fibre content must appear in the official language of the country of sale. Plan multilingual labels before expanding into new EU markets.', null));
    if (answers['q14'] === 'no') actions.push(buildAction('warning', 'Arrange a social compliance audit (BSCI or SEDEX/SMETA)', 'Most EU retailers and marketplaces request a current social audit during supplier onboarding.', '/contact'));
    if (answers['q15'] === 'no' || answers['q15'] === 'partial') actions.push(buildAction('warning', 'Confirm you are claiming Bangladesh EBA 0% duty', 'Bangladesh-made garments can enter the EU duty-free under EBA. Check your factory is providing GSP Form A or REX origin documents with each shipment.', null));
    if (answers['q10'] === 'no') actions.push(buildAction('warning', 'Start recording material composition data per style', 'DPP enforcement for textiles is expected from around 2027–2028. Begin tracking fibre percentages, fabric mill, and origin now.', null));
    if (answers['q4'] === 'no') actions.push(buildAction('warning', 'Add lot or style codes to garment labels', 'A style code plus season code on the care label meets the GPSR traceability minimum.', null));
    if (answers['q18'] === 'no') actions.push(buildAction('warning', 'Write a one-page safety complaints and recall procedure', 'GPSR expects a basic documented process for handling safety complaints and product withdrawals.', null));

    if (actions.length === 0) {
      actions.push(buildAction('ok', 'Your compliance foundation looks strong', 'Keep documentation current, renew certifications annually, and watch for the finalised Digital Product Passport rules expected in 2026–2027.', null));
    }

    actions.sort((a, b) => {
      if (a.priority === 'critical' && b.priority !== 'critical') return -1;
      if (a.priority !== 'critical' && b.priority === 'critical') return 1;
      return 0;
    });

    const actionListEl = document.getElementById('action-list');
    actionListEl.innerHTML = '';
    actions.slice(0, 8).forEach((action) => {
      const iconClass = action.priority === 'critical' ? 'critical' : action.priority === 'warning' ? 'warning' : 'ok';
      const symbol = action.priority === 'critical' ? '!' : action.priority === 'warning' ? '▲' : '✓';

      const item = document.createElement('div');
      item.className = 'action-item';

      const icon = document.createElement('div');
      icon.className = 'action-icon ' + iconClass;
      icon.textContent = symbol;

      const textWrap = document.createElement('div');

      const titleEl = document.createElement('div');
      titleEl.className = 'action-title';
      titleEl.textContent = action.title;

      const descEl = document.createElement('div');
      descEl.className = 'action-desc';
      descEl.textContent = action.description;

      if (action.link) {
        descEl.append(' ');
        const linkEl = document.createElement('a');
        linkEl.href = action.link;
        linkEl.className = 'action-link';
        linkEl.textContent = 'SDF can help →';
        descEl.appendChild(linkEl);
      }

      textWrap.appendChild(titleEl);
      textWrap.appendChild(descEl);
      item.appendChild(icon);
      item.appendChild(textWrap);
      actionListEl.appendChild(item);
    });

    const criticalCount = actions.filter((a) => a.priority === 'critical').length;
    if (criticalCount > 0) {
      const plural = criticalCount > 1 ? 's' : '';
      document.getElementById('cta-text').textContent =
        'You have ' + criticalCount + ' critical compliance gap' + plural + ' to address before selling into the EU. ' +
        'SDF Clothing is GOTS, OEKO-TEX, and BSCI certified — we provide compliance-relevant documentation with every confirmed order.';
    }

    const resultsEl = document.getElementById('results');
    resultsEl.classList.add('visible');
    resultsEl.scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' });
  });
</script>

</BaseLayout>
